; final polls holding above six points would confirm the current picture.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff seeks a second term against Representative Mike Collins in a state that narrowly favored Republicans at the presidential level. Every recent poll shows Ossoff ahead, with margins ranging from four to eleven points, including surveys from Republican-affiliated pollsters. Averages of published polls place his lead near eight and a half points in the final weeks of the campaign.\n\nOssoff holds an overwhelming financial advantage, having raised roughly ten times as much as Collins and entering the homestretch with about $15 million on hand. Race raters overwhelmingly classify the contest as Likely Democratic, and prediction markets give Ossoff roughly a 94 to 96 percent chance of winning. Collins benefits from outside groups running attacks, but the late polling trend has been stable. The race remains a clear Ossoff advantage, with the main uncertainty being turnout and any late shift among undecided voters.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9522, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9478, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9479, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9545, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.928, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9516, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9505, "marg